{"id":"6994aafd3bf766a5","group":"58","path":"58/batch09/58-df-reflection-principle.md","title":"Reflection Principle","display":"df-reflection-principle — Reflection Principle","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-reflection-principle","aliases":["58-df-reflection-principle"],"display":"df-reflection-principle — Reflection Principle","depends_on":["[[58-df-ordinal]]","[[58-df-hierarchy]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-reflection-principle"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-reflection-principle</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-reflection-principle — Reflection Principle"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"58-df-ordinal\">58-df-ordinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"19e9a8c33d5c841c\" href=\"?note=19e9a8c33d5c841c\" title=\"58-df-hierarchy\">58-df-hierarchy</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)\">\\(\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi(x_0,\\ldots,x_{n-1})\">\\(\\varphi(x_0,\\ldots,x_{n-1})\\)</span> is a metalinguistic formula of set theory and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi^{V_\\beta}\">\\(\\varphi^{V_\\beta}\\)</span> is its usual relativization to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V_\\beta\">\\(V_\\beta\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ReflectionInstance}\">\\(\\mathrm{ReflectionInstance}\\)</span> is a metalinguistic schema abbreviation, not an object-language truth predicate</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflection\\text{-}principle} \\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}} \\mathrm{ReflectionInstance}(\\varphi,n,\\alpha)\\Longleftrightarrow \\exists\\beta\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\beta)\\land\\alpha\\in\\beta\\land\\forall\\bar a\\in V_\\beta^n\\;\\bigl(\\varphi(\\bar a)\\leftrightarrow\\varphi^{V_\\beta}(\\bar a)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflection\\text{-}principle} \\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}} \\mathrm{ReflectionInstance}(\\varphi,n,\\alpha)\\Longleftrightarrow \\exists\\beta\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\beta)\\land\\alpha\\in\\beta\\land\\forall\\bar a\\in V_\\beta^n\\;\\bigl(\\varphi(\\bar a)\\leftrightarrow\\varphi^{V_\\beta}(\\bar a)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The displayed line is an external schema. It deliberately does not introduce a set-coded truth predicate for the proper class <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The reflection principle states that every fixed formula has arbitrarily high reflecting ranks.</li>\n<li>For any finite set of formulas and any <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta\">\\(\\theta\\)</span>, there exists <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha &gt; \\theta\">\\(\\alpha &gt; \\theta\\)</span> such that the formulas reflect to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V_{\\alpha}\">\\(V_{\\alpha}\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-ordinal","status":"resolved","id":"5582a281f15a33c2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-ordinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-hierarchy","status":"resolved","id":"19e9a8c33d5c841c","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-hierarchy]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi(x_0,\\ldots,x_{n-1})","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi^{V_\\beta}","display":false},{"tex":"V_\\beta","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ReflectionInstance}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflection\\text{-}principle} \\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}} \\mathrm{ReflectionInstance}(\\varphi,n,\\alpha)\\Longleftrightarrow \\exists\\beta\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\beta)\\land\\alpha\\in\\beta\\land\\forall\\bar a\\in V_\\beta^n\\;\\bigl(\\varphi(\\bar a)\\leftrightarrow\\varphi^{V_\\beta}(\\bar a)\\bigr)\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"V","display":false},{"tex":"\\theta","display":false},{"tex":"\\alpha > \\theta","display":false},{"tex":"V_{\\alpha}","display":false}],"bytes":1344,"backlinks":[{"id":"dea0e944a5a296c9","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1057","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-reflection-principle.md|58-df-reflection-principle]]（batch09）"}],"outgoing":["5582a281f15a33c2","19e9a8c33d5c841c"]}